# Node: direct closed calculation; exact radical
# Before (rejected by the baseline release):
# sqrt(1/9)=1/3
# Former behavior: JSON success=false and process exit 1.
# Now: the same assertion and its exact eval are supported.
# Boundary: false results and ill-defined inputs still reject; see
# examples/negative/closed_exact_elementary_calculation/.
# Run: target/release/litex -strict -f examples/proof_nodes/equal/by_builtin_rule/closed_radical_calculation.lit

sqrt(1/9)=1/3
sqrt(4/9)=2/3
sqrt(8)=2*sqrt(2)
sqrt(12)+sqrt(27)=5*sqrt(3)
sqrt(12)-sqrt(27)=-sqrt(3)
sqrt(1/2)=sqrt(2)/2
sqrt(2)*sqrt(8)=4
sqrt(2)*sqrt(3)=sqrt(6)
1/sqrt(2)=sqrt(2)/2
sqrt(2)^3=2*sqrt(2)
(3-2*sqrt(2))*(3+2*sqrt(2))=1
sqrt(2)+sqrt(3) != sqrt(5)
eval sqrt(1/9)
eval sqrt(12)+sqrt(27)
eval 1/sqrt(2)
